Mark XXI: the dashboard becomes the full agent console

The console tab previously ran a plain chat completion - no tools, no
gate. It now runs the SAME agent as the CLI: all 24 tools, the same
confirmation gate, the same persona and system prompt.

- dashboard.py: DashboardState rebuilt on the Mark IX bridge pattern,
  minus the network - 127.0.0.1 only, no token. POST /api/chat starts a
  worker-thread turn; progress flows as events (user/status/
  confirm_request/reply) polled from GET /api/events (bounded long-poll);
  POST /api/confirm answers the gate (120s timeout = denied). Registry
  honors the same LITE/PRO flags as the CLI (screen control, watchtower).
  One turn at a time (409 when busy); events capped at 600.
- Mark XV parity: every dashboard turn is logged to the local
  conversation store as a "Dashboard session", so /history and
  history_search see web-console turns too.
- dashboard_page.py: chat tab rewired to the event stream - tool status
  lines, the reply stream, and an in-browser APPROVE/DENY banner; the
  event poll starts at boot and survives tab switches.
- Settings save rebuilds the agent's brain chain (previous behavior
  preserved: blank key field keeps the stored key).
- Tests: full round-trip with a fake brain chain and a custom gated tool
  - approve path (confirm_request -> approve -> reply + status line),
  deny path (refusal -> BLOCKED reply), memory/kanban/license endpoints
  alongside the agent, conversation-store logging, settings key
  preservation; page markers now include /api/events, /api/confirm,
  APPROVE/DENY.
- Version 3.8.0.
